  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 configurations (config_041: 0.725, config_039: 0.721, config_008: 0.706) all use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + multimodal, with transformer aggregation and weighted/concat fusion. Transformer > avgpool (0.725 vs 0.706) and weighted ≈ concat (0.725 vs 0.721) are well-supported. config_044 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) is the only remaining untested configuration within this proven high-performing encoder/profile region. Question: Does the transformer aggregation advantage persist under concat fusion, or could avgpool+concat be a competitive (and potentially cheaper) alternative? This is the best use of experiment 9 because (a) it is the closest untested variant to the current best, giving the highest probability of a competitive result, (b) it reduces residual uncertainty about whether the 0.725 ceiling is truly set or whether a different aggregation-fusion pairing could close the gap, and (c) it informs the final experiment: if it lands near 0.72, the last slot can be spent on a targeted refinement; if it drops significantly, it confirms config_041 as the robust optimum. Expected cost: moderate, roughly 4–5 GPU hours (avgpool is cheaper than transformer, but ViT-L image encoding and multiprofile aggregation keep it comparable to config_008's 4.82 hrs)."
}

